  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as in step 1; none added or dropped.",
   "Circuit: 5V \u2192 + rail \u2192 photoresistor \u2192 junction (column 12) \u2192 A0 and 10k resistor \u2192 GND via the - rail. Pin 9 \u2192 220 ohm resistor \u2192 LED anode; LED cathode \u2192 GND via the - rail.",
   "The circuit image is cropped, so the breadboard columns are my own choice. The connections follow the tutorial text and the visible wires.",
   "I assumed the short blue wire in the image carries pin 9 to the 220 ohm resistor, because the pin 9 wire is not visible in the crop.",
   "The 220 ohm resistor is on the LED anode side, with the LED cathode going to ground.",
   "The schematic image did not load. The potentiometer on analog input 2 mentioned in the text is only an alternative sensor, so it is not built."
  ]
 },
